WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.261
Picture a night in
a small town in Tamil Nadu.

2
00:00:03.261 --> 00:00:08.451
A woman is in pain, and her daughter turns
to the local health worker with a

3
00:00:08.451 --> 00:00:09.680
question in Tamil.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.086
Her pain is worse
at night. What should we do?

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.833
Palli Sahayak is a voice assistant
for palliative care, and it's open source.

6
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:25.386
You ask out loud, in your own
language, by an ordinary phone call,

7
00:00:25.386 --> 00:00:28.284
WhatsApp, or the web. No new app to learn.

8
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.390
It works like an open-book exam:
it first looks the question up in a small,

9
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.456
curated library of palliative care guidance,
then gives a short spoken answer,

10
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:41.079
built from what it found.

11
00:00:42.387 --> 00:00:46.807
Here's a short excerpt from a completely
fictional conversation: made up,

12
00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:48.019
with no real people.

13
00:00:50.854 --> 00:00:52.931
A daughter, in Tamil.

14
00:00:53.454 --> 00:00:55.694
Caregiver (daughter): Yes, they have.

15
00:00:55.694 --> 00:01:00.718
But… we only give it when the pain comes, the
lady next door said she'd get used to

16
00:01:00.718 --> 00:01:00.900
it.

17
00:01:02.087 --> 00:01:06.931
Palli Sahayak: Give it just
as the doctor said. If times are set,

18
00:01:06.931 --> 00:01:11.254
don't wait for the pain.
Don't change the amount yourself;

19
00:01:11.254 --> 00:01:13.714
if you're unsure, ask the doctor.

20
00:01:14.687 --> 00:01:18.156
Palli Sahayak: Talk
to your nurse or doctor today.

21
00:01:18.156 --> 00:01:20.724
If the pain suddenly gets much worse,

22
00:01:20.724 --> 00:01:26.414
call 108 for emergency help right away, and
tell your nurse too. You're not alone.

23
00:01:29.253 --> 00:01:33.410
Notice the guard rails. It
never gives specific medicine doses.

24
00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:38.688
If it hears danger signs, it tells
the caller to call one zero eight right away,

25
00:01:38.688 --> 00:01:42.251
and flags the call as
urgent for clinicians to review.

26
00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:49.013
Palli Sahayak is an ongoing project,
supported by the Gates Foundation and BIRAC.

27
00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:52.094
It has not yet been
tested with real patients.

28
00:01:52.094 --> 00:01:57.386
The code is open for anyone to read and use,
and the full video tells the whole

29
00:01:57.386 --> 00:01:57.788
story.
